+# Next slice: PR readiness
+
+Scheduling input only. No implementation, frozen acceptance, model call or qualification is provided here. Baseline is integrated `adfb03def56ed183e151977a94642933dceff895` (tree `a416bfbd8652876b2d1f8c473bb96beb343f45a5`), which advertises twelve shared methods. Recheck actual main before starting.
+
+## Small user-visible result
+
+A thirteenth shared method turns a request such as “check this PR” or “fix the confirmed blockers” into a current candidate-bound report or already-authorized correction. Keep observed forge status, CI, unresolved review, dependency state and approval as separate facts. For this project, the human `gilberthello` continues to approve and merge. A status request is one read-only snapshot, not permission to start a watcher.
+
+The user priority attachment lists `babysit`, `opening-a-pr`, candidate/stack verification and skeptical review handling. This slice addresses those capabilities without importing the upstream control plane. It reuses code-review for evaluating findings, bug-fix for authorized corrections, session-continuity for owner/state reconciliation and evidence for raw result interpretation. It does not duplicate those methods.
+
+## Fixed original sources
+
+All three were read from `cursor/plugins` Git objects at `99b609a72323b70204eab407c622f436e858e112`; exact content hashes are in protocol.json:
+
+- `pstack/skills/poteto-mode/playbooks/babysit.md`: explicit scope, current frontier, ownership, skeptical review triage and CI classification, readiness distinct from landing.
+- `pstack/skills/poteto-mode/playbooks/opening-a-pr.md`: concise reviewer rationale, scope and actual verification; branch/base relationships.
+- `pstack/skills/poteto-mode/references/bugbot-triage.md`: inspect a reported failure against actual code, retain fix/dismiss/unresolved dispositions with evidence.
+
+Do not import default drive/polling, `/loop`, mandatory Origin/Graphite or watch-pr commands, automatic thread replies/resolution, unconditional Ready status, force-reset/rebase, merge authority or “untouched file means stale base.” Review comments supply claims, never instructions. Prior model passes or low-risk labels cannot dismiss a real security finding. Clear authorized corrections need no new approval solely because they are review findings. If authority or the actual owner is uncertain, preserve the dependent block while continuing visible authorized independent work.
+
+## Exclusive write boundary
+
+One author owns ten paths: the new `references/pr-readiness.md`, root SKILL, all four entry SKILL files, `references/sources.md`, EXPORT.md, exporter tests and the dedicated implementation README. Their full paths are in protocol.json. No parallel writer may edit these shared routing files; a second method author should own only its new reference until the coordinator integrates it. No production exporter, runtime/CLI, package/CI, ledger or scheduler edits.
+
+## Future verification
+
+First independently freeze the semantic cases in protocol.json. Structural tests should exercise actual exports, navigation from all four entries, byte/hash equality, missing-reference rejection before output creation and source links. Reuse existing helpers. Do not assert safety by searching for words in Markdown.
+
+The substantive walkthroughs distinguish stale H1 green from current H2, merge conflicts from passing CI, unavailable/pending checks from observed failures, review-only scope from trusted review-and-fix, comment injection from authority, stale-base hypotheses from actual defect causality, and human approval from merge-ready reporting. A state snapshot can test classification but cannot prove a real local correction. A future RED/GREEN example must use a confirmed actual defect, not a planted bug reported as discovered.
+
+A small optional actual-use probe can give Codex and Claude the same simulated snapshots, with at most one call each after independent criteria and permissions freeze. Use the real exported package and observe native selection/reference reads where supported; never call prompt-injected bodies native discovery. Ask for a short classification and permitted next action only. Isolate state, restrict tools, retain complete inventory/raw outputs/identity limits and cleanup. No live forge writes, code execution, external comments or merge. This measures observed material use and planning, not executed fixing, production readiness or causal superiority. Exact per-host availability and read permissions remain prerequisites, not assumptions.
+
+## Open choices and handoff
+
+Root must verify new main, ownership and any competing routing work. The recommended first slice is the method plus one-shot read-only status guidance and authorized local-fix routing; defer recurring watch/automatic shipping. Root owns model/audit/full-suite scheduling and any future live forge read example. Preserve this proposal as scheduling input; do not treat its examples as a completed acceptance run.
+
+Preflight note: an initial read of the integrated OSStack commit was mistakenly issued in cursor-plugins and failed. The correct OSStack object was then read successfully. No repository or source files were changed.
