+# PR-readiness host probe — bounded observations
+
+Both hosts received the same four synthetic PR snapshots and read-only classification request from author candidate `95a33e371464fe48bf063afe17ed650852e925d5`. The ten integrated author paths at root candidate `c95dccd01a884e84e413817c338f2303ed02a9a7` are byte-identical; `candidate-bindings.json` records that separate Git comparison. This does not turn the probe into an execution on live main.
+
+Initial 048 preparation was superseded before any model user turn; its zero-turn metadata and original files are preserved. HR01–HR12 expectations are unchanged; a prospective supplement rebinds the source and index pin to 95a33e before any answer. The independent reviewer is another agent, not a formally independent trusted principal. Final-context checks, this supplement and root dispatch preceded both calls. Each host received one user turn, 180 seconds model wait and zero retries; termination grace is separate.
+
+## Semantic classification
+
+Both answers classify A pending/stale checks and approval, B current explicit-zero failure plus an untrusted instruction, C changed-base conflict despite green checks, and D snapshot-only merge readiness with a human merge owner. These are supplied synthetic facts, not live PR observations or newly reproduced defects.
+
+Independent agent grading is **Codex LIMITED** and **Claude FAILED**. Both B plans omit explicit rebinding of future results to the corrected candidate. Claude also does not explicitly plan executing the same-trigger verification, mentioning restoration and adding/keeping a test instead. Correct main classifications do not close these plan details. The original criteria, supplement and scores are preserved.
+
+## Format and final selection
+
